  "text": "Recipe: Air Fried Masala Vada\nCreator: Dr Sirisha Potluri\nCategory: Snack\nIngredients: 1 cup chana dal (soaked for 5-6 hours, washed & drained), 1 cup grated potatoes, microwaved or steamed, 1 bunch cilantro, thinly diced, 1 bunch mint, thinly diced, 5-6 medium spiced green chilies, thinly sliced, 1 medium sized red onion, diced, 1/4 cup curry leaves, chopped, 2-3 inches ginger, grated, 1 tsp turmeric powder, 1 Tbsp black peppercorns, coarsely ground, Salt to taste [optional]\nCooking methods: pulse, mix, air-fry, soak, microwave, steam\nInstructions: BATTER: In a food processor, pulse chana dal into a coarse mixture. Add the rest of the ingredients except grated potatoes. Pulse a few times so that everything mixes well. Then add grated potatoes (microwaved or steamed). Mix well. VADA: Make even sized balls, then shape them into vadas (see pic). Air fry both sides at 350 F for 7 minutes and 3 minutes, respectively, flipping them over in between.\nNotes: A recipe with BEANS (chana dal), TUBERS (potatoes), HERBS & SPICES (various).",
